79:A total of 218 healthy CTRL and 79 patients were included  in  the  longitudinal  analysis  (table  1  and  supplementary  figures  1  and  8).  There  was  no  significant difference  either  in  the  number  of  contacts  with  the healthcare system for ICD-10 classified 'Mental, Behavioral  and  Neurodevelopmental  disorders,'  nor  in duration of contacts with the healthcare system (e.g., the duration of treatment) between the longitudinal sample and the drop-outs. There was no significant association between  attrition  groups  and  PANSS  scores,  or  median  cortical  deviation  scores.  Data  on  medication  use for  each  timepoint  showed that patients primarily used second-generation antipsychotics (62% at baseline, 48% at 1 year, and 17% at 10 years) or did not use any antipsychotics (38%, 50%, and 83%, respectively; for details, see supplementary material).
